# Personal commit blocklist — TEMPLATE.
#
# Copy this to `.commit-blocklist` (which is gitignored) and put your own
# sensitive strings there. A staged change that ADDS matching content blocks the
# commit. Keep real values only in `.commit-blocklist`, never in this template.
#
# Rule kinds (one per line; blank lines and `#` comments ignored):
#
#   foo             BLOCK — case-insensitive literal substring
#                   (dots in a domain or IP are literal, not regex).
#   re:<pattern>    BLOCK — case-insensitive regex. Use for word-bounded names
#                   so a short name doesn't over-match:  re:\bJane Doe\b
#   !foo  /  !re:…  ALLOW (gitignore-style `!`). Un-blocks a match whose span sits
#                   inside the allow match's span — block broadly, carve out a
#                   legit use:  block `Marlowe`, then `!@marlowe` to permit the
#                   npm scope. A blocked term elsewhere on the line still fires
#                   (you can't smuggle one in beside an allowed token).
#   file:<glob>     IGNORE a whole file. `*` matches within a path segment, `**`
#                   across `/`; a glob with no `/` matches by basename at any
#                   depth, so `file:package.json` exempts every package.json.
#                   COARSE — it blinds the guard to the entire file, so prefer a
#                   `!` allow for a specific token when you can.
#
# Behavior:
#   - No `.commit-blocklist` file => silent no-op (opt-in per person).
#   - A malformed list (bad regex) => the commit fails closed.
#   - Only STAGED ADDITIONS are scanned, so pre-existing content never blocks you.
#   - Reports file:line + the blocklist ENTRY NUMBER, never the matched value, so
#     it can't re-leak what you block. Look an entry up with:
#         sed -n '<N>p' .commit-blocklist
#   - `git commit --no-verify` bypasses it (convenience, not enforcement).
#
# Example entries (illustrative — delete, and add your own in .commit-blocklist):
#   example.internal.host
#   203.0.113.10
#   re:\bYour Name\b
#   !@yourscope
#   file:package.json
